      "applicability": "not_applicable",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C30", "C31", "C33", "C35", "C37", "C38", "C39", "C40", "C41", "C42"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability data exist for the query molecule.",
    "The closest analog (verapamil) F is borderline (22%, 95% CI 17–29%); the query's cyclic 1,3-dithiane 1,1,3,3-tetraoxide modification increases polarity and size, but its effect on F is unquantified.",
    "No query-specific data on absorption, first-pass metabolism, efflux, solubility, or formulation are available.",
    "Verapamil cirrhosis records are internally inconsistent (22% vs 52.3%), but both are ≥20%; this does not affect the threshold decision.",
    "Sub-20% F values in other species/scaffolds (mouse venlafaxine, rat sulpiride, dog tramadol SR) are not transferable to the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F≥20%) because the most transferable evidence, verapamil absolute oral bioavailability of 22% in fasted volunteers, supports the threshold, and no affirmative low-F evidence exists for the query; the low physicochemical prior is uncertain and not sufficient to override the close-analog experimental outcome. New L2 verapamil records (22% and 52.3%) are consistent with ≥20% and do not overturn the prior decision."
}

